e_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#a--code-shipped-dev-merge-or-push-to-main","content":"A — Code shipped (`~/dev/*` merge or push to `main`)"},"1959":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-5","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#b--jackie-os--vault--system-only","content":"B — Jackie-OS / vault / `System/` only"},"1960":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-6","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#c--sergei-reports-admin--life-items-done-no-code","content":"C — Sergei reports admin / life items done (no code)"},"1961":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-7","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#d--do-not-sync-common-mistakes","content":"D — Do **not** sync (common mistakes)"},"1962":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-8","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#roadmap-reconcile","content":"Roadmap reconcile"},"1963":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-9","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"When to run"},"1964":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-10","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"Catalog cleanup"},"1965":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-11","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#steps","content":"Steps"},"1966":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-12","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#process","content":"Process"},"1967":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-13","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#rules","content":"Rules"},"1968":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-14","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up","content":"**Purpose:** close a working session — capture what changed, keep the vault and git in sync."},"1969":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-15","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up","content":"**Triggers:** `/wrap-up&#x60; · &#x2A;*`/wrap-up all`*&#x2A; (multi-session catch-up) · &#x2A;*`/wrap-up merge`** (PR ship first) · `wrap up` · `session end` · user marks work **done** · agent finishes implementation (proactive). Also run after a code-repo merge or direct push to `main` (manual — no Cursor automation). Backstops: **07:30 morning-brief** · merge-poll (\\~2h) — see Cheat sheet."},"1970":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-16","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up","content":"**Not this skill:*&#x2A; &#x2A;*`sync projects`** alone → project-sync only (no ops kanban, no full hot rewrite, **no git push**)."},"1971":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-17","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up","content":"**Agent contract:** when you **finish implementation** (shipped code, merged PR, completed vault/system work, or Sergei reports something done) — **do not stop at the code diff**. Run this checklist in the **same session** unless Sergei explicitly says to skip. Leaving `hot.md`, today's brief, or project `## Status` stale is a failed handoff."},"1972":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-18","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up","content":"**Tomorrow's brief contract:** anything you'd expect in tomorrow morning's **Since last brief · Work*&#x2A; section must land in a dated **`## Status` prepend tonight*&#x2A; (use &#x2A;*`Shipped:`*&#x2A; / &#x2A;*`Next:`*&#x2A; / &#x2A;*`Blocked:`*&#x2A; sub-lines when the session shipped code). Plus brief &#x2A;*`## Log`**. `hot.md` is current-focus only. Morning-brief synthesizes **Since last brief** from Status prepends, merge-poll, and git delta — not from hot or memory."},"1973":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-19","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"Vault sync reads &#x2A;*`origin/&#60;branch>`** — unpushed commits don't exist for project-sync or tomorrow's brief."},"1974":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-20","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"Mode"},"1975":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-21","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"Trigger"},"1976":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-22","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"When to use"},"1977":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-23","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"**Direct** (default)"},"1978":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-24","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"`/wrap-up` · `/wrap-up all`"},"1979":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-25","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"Work already on `main`/`master`, or solo-maintainer **direct push** after verify"},"1980":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-26","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"**PR**"},"1981":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-27","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"`/wrap-up merge` · `wrap up merge`"},"1982":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-28","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"Session ended on a **feature branch** — open PR, squash-merge, then vault sync"},"1983":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-29","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"**Commit only**"},"1984":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-30","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"`wrap up no push` (explicit)"},"1985":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-31","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"Rare — offline / draft handoff; **flag unpushed** in report"},"1986":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-32","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"**Default:** every `/wrap-up&#x60; ends with Jackie-OS &#x2A;*`git commit` + `git push`** to `origin/master`. Never force-push."},"1987":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-33","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"**Order:** finish all code-repo ships (direct or PR) **before** Jackie-OS project-sync — vault Status must reference merged SHAs on `origin/main`."},"1988":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-34","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#compound-check--gate-before-vault-sync","content":"After the code ships and **before** project-sync, ask **silently** (no need to call it out): did this session produce a **reusable technique, root-caused bug, or hard-won insight** — something a future agent couldn't reconstruct from the diff? (typo, rename, boilerplate ship, version bump → No. Novel pattern, subtle root cause, non-obvious gotcha → Yes.)"},"1989":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-35","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#compound-check--gate-before-vault-sync","content":"**Yes →** run `jos-compound` now, while context is hot (`docs/solutions/` + agent-learnings-index row). Don't defer it to a cron/Action — a cold post-merge job can't know what you tried or whether the fix was worth documenting. State the intent once; don't ask permission."},"1990":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-36","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#compound-check--gate-before-vault-sync","content":"**No →** skip silently. Most sessions don't warrant it. **Do not offer jos-compound proactively after every ship** — the gate is a private judgment call. If unsure, the answer is No."},"1991":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-37","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#after-implementation--checklist","content":"Use this when work is **done**, not only when Sergei says \"wrap up\"."},"1992":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-38","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#a--code-shipped-dev-merge-or-push-to-main","content":"**In the code repo:** verification passed; &#x2A;*commit + push to `main`/`master`** (default) **or*&#x2A; PR merged via &#x2A;*`/wrap-up merge`**. See § Git ship modes."},"1993":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-39","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#a--code-shipped-dev-merge-or-push-to-main","content":"**jos-compound** — run the Compound check above."},"1994":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-40","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#a--code-shipped-dev-merge-or-push-to-main","content":"**Roadmap reconcile gate** — if a **tracked plan / initiative** finished or advanced, or shipped work overlaps the idea catalog: § Roadmap reconcile + § Catalog cleanup in that repo (commit + push **in the code repo**). Includes: **CHANGELOG** § Unreleased for Newfin and the **litmus** (live `plans/` = only active files; `git rm` anything ✅/superseded/deferred-indefinitely). Skip only for drive-by fixes with no plan and no catalog overlap. Draw: skip (vault only).\r\n3b. **Linear-tracked repo** — if the code repo has `docs/linear-workflow.md` (currently **bunit*&#x2A;), follow its **§ Sync contract** with Linear: move shipped issues → `Done` (verify GitHub sync didn't already), new bugs/ideas → `Backlog` (`AI Refinement`). **Posting a Linear project status update is automated** — the Hermes merge-poll cron does it for any batch of ≥2 merged commits on a `docs/linear-workflow.md` repo. Only post one yourself if the session's merge was a single commit (below the cron's threshold) or you can see the cron's post failed. The catalog for these repos is Linear, not `future-improvements.md`. Skip silently for repos without that file."},"1995":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-41","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#a--code-shipped-dev-merge-or-push-to-main","content":"**From Jackie-OS:** project-sync → prepend `Vault/{Newfin,Rodyna,Draw}.md` `## Status` → rebuild `hot.md` active lines → append today's brief `## Log` → fix any **stale claims** you know are wrong in brief/hot (e.g. \"migration pending\" when GHA auto-applies; \"P1 in progress\" when roadmap index says ✅ shipped). On **heavy code days** (≥15 commits or multiple themes in one session), the vault Status prepend should be **thematic*&#x2A; with explicit &#x2A;*`Shipped:`*&#x2A; / &#x2A;*`Next:`*&#x2A; / &#x2A;*`Blocked:`*&#x2A; sub-lines. Add &#x2A;*`## Since sync`** to today's brief when the session contradicts morning **Projects** or **Since last brief · Work** (all active code projects, not Jackie-OS only)."},"1996":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-42","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#a--code-shipped-dev-merge-or-push-to-main","content":"**Jackie-OS plans:** if a `System/plans/` item shipped → § Roadmap reconcile (Jackie-OS system plans).\r\n5b. **Docs sync** — if the ship added/changed a skill, script, worker agent, connector, or architecture-level behavior: update the owning doc per the ownership map (CATALOG for skills/scripts, CONCEPTS for vocabulary, ARCHITECTURE for system shape) **in the same commit**. The docs-first gate only works if docs stay true."},"1997":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-43","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#b--jackie-os--vault--system-only","content":"**Status:** if focus, blockers, or next actions shifted → prepend relevant vault note `## Status` (e.g. Jackie OS, project notes)."},"1998":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-44","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#b--jackie-os--vault--system-only","content":"**B-Unit visit (Jul 2–22):** if Sergei reported execution → append today's bullets to matching `Projects/B-Unit/curriculum/week-*/day-NN.md&#x60; **## Done**; run `python3 System/capture/b_unit_day_log_sync.py` if journal used `B-Unit:` prefix."},"1999":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-45","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#b--jackie-os--vault--system-only","content":"**Brief:** append `## Log&#x60;; clear inbox/carried items Sergei marked done; add &#x2A;*`## Since sync`** if evening session contradicts morning brief **Projects**, **Since last brief**, or **Today** (one short corrective block per affected project — applies after code-repo sprints too). On sprint days, prefer one **themed** Log line over ten sha lines."},"2000":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-46","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#b--jackie-os--vault--system-only","content":"**hot.md:** full overwrite (\\~500 words) when priorities/blockers changed."},"2001":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-47","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#b--jackie-os--vault--system-only","content":"**Plans/skills:** shipped plan → § Roadmap reconcile (Jackie-OS system plans); retired skill → pointer in Skills Registry. If Jackie-OS surface changed materially (projects, automations, teach tracks) → refresh the shareable explainer.\r\n5b. &#x2A;*Skill feedback (capture, then offer):** if a **skill** under- or over-performed this session and Sergei corrected its output, append one `open` row to skill-feedback (date · skill · signal · `session` · open). &#x2A;*If you appended a row this session, offer once:** \"want me to draft a skill-improve diff for \\<skill> now, or leave it for Sunday?\" — on yes, draft the diff for approval; on no, it waits for the weekly curator pass. Never edit the skill unprompted. Skip the whole step silently if no skill misbehaved."},"2002":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-48","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#b--jackie-os--vault--system-only","content":"**Commit + push** Jackie-OS touched files (`origin/master`). Skip push only when Sergei explicitly says so."},"2003":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-49","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#c--sergei-reports-admin--life-items-done-no-code","content":"Remove from today's brief inbox/carried lines."},"2004":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-50","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#c--sergei-reports-admin--life-items-done-no-code","content":"Log under `## Log` with timestamp."},"2005":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-51","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#c--sergei-reports-admin--life-items-done-no-code","content":"Commit if brief changed."},"2006":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-52","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#d--do-not-sync-common-mistakes","content":"Situation"},"2007":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-53","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#d--do-not-sync-common-mistakes","content":"Action"},"2008":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-54","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#d--do-not-sync-common-mistakes","content":"Vault-only doc edit that doesn't change project state"},"2009":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-55","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#d--do-not-sync-common-mistakes","content":"Commit only; skip full project-sync"},"2010":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-56","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#d--do-not-sync-common-mistakes","content":"Routine typo in a skill"},"2011":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-57","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#d--do-not-sync-common-mistakes","content":"Commit; refresh `hot.md` only if priorities shifted"},"2012":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-58","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#d--do-not-sync-common-mistakes","content":"Code merged but you're still in the code repo"},"2013":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-59","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#d--do-not-sync-common-mistakes","content":"Switch to Jackie-OS and finish § A.3–A.5 before ending"},"2014":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-60","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#roadmap-reconcile","content":"After a **realized plan** ships on `main`, update that project's roadmap index and plan docs **in the same session** — before project-sync. Morning-brief syncs vault, not `plans/`."},"2015":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-61","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Shipped"},"2016":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-62","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Run?"},"2017":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-63","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Last task of a dated plan / initiative on `main`"},"2018":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-64","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Yes**"},"2019":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-65","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Partial slice (open phases remain)"},"2020":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-66","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Yes** — mark 🔵 partial + what's next"},"2021":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-67","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Bugfix / chore with no plan doc"},"2022":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-68","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**No**"},"2023":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-69","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Shipped slice maps to `future-improvements.md` (with or without a dated plan)"},"2024":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-70","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Yes** — § Catalog cleanup required"},"2025":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-71","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Jackie-OS `System/plans/` item"},"2026":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-72","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Yes** — see Jackie-OS system plans below"},"2027":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-73","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Roadmap paths** — `System/project-registry.md` **Roadmap index** column (not hardcoded in skills)."},"2028":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-74","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Owned code repos** — ground truth is code, migrations, merged PRs — not plan banners or `- [ ]` boxes. Verification depth: Newfin `docs/solutions/workflow-issues/verify-plan-status-against-ground-truth.md` (same rules in any repo)."},"2029":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-75","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Identify the plan (roadmap-linked initiative or implementation plan you finished)."},"2030":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-76","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Verify: grep promised artifacts; `git log` since plan date; **code wins** over stale headers/checkboxes."},"2031":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-77","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Update roadmap index: `_Last audited against main on YYYY-MM-DD (HEAD …)_`; row → ✅ shipped · 🔵 partial · 📋 idea · ⏸ deferred; refresh \"remaining surface\" / next-work blurb if present."},"2032":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-78","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Update plan doc header (`> Status: ✅ shipped …` or partial). Index is the live board — don't mass-tick body checkboxes unless auditing the whole doc."},"2033":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-79","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Delete-on-ship when fully realized (2026-06-29 policy).** Capture the deliverable in `roadmap-index.md` § Shipped (+ `CHANGELOG` for Newfin) and any durable decision in `decisions-log.md&#x60;, then **`git rm` the dated plan body** — no `archive/` of full bodies; git history is the audit trail. Repoint any links into the deleted file (to the ledgers / live skills / `docs/solutions/&#x60;). Never delete idea catalogs or the two ledgers. &#x2A;(Rodyna's existing `plans/archive/implemented/` predates this policy — sweep it on its next ship.)*"},"2034":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-80","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Catalog cleanup** — same commit when the ship touches catalog lines."},"2035":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-81","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Litmus (run before commit, every repo touched).** The live `plans/` folder must contain **only** `roadmap-index.md`, `decisions-log.md`, `future-improvements.md`, `README.md`, and **active** dated plans. Grep each remaining live plan against its roadmap row: anything marked ✅ shipped / ⤴ superseded / ⏸ deferred-indefinitely should be **deleted** (after the two ledgers capture it), not left live. This catches the easy miss where a row gets flipped to ✅ but the file lingers."},"2036":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-82","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Commit in the **code repo** — `docs(plans): reconcile &#60;plan> shipped on &#60;sha>` (or `… catalog after &#60;topic>`) — push before Jackie-OS project-sync."},"2037":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-83","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Jackie-OS system plans:** update Roadmap § Shipped + Decisions log + Ideas backlog; fold durable rules into skills or root `CLAUDE.md&#x60;; **`git rm` the shipped plan body** (git history keeps it); commit in Jackie-OS."},"2038":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-84","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"**Required in the same session** whenever shipped code realizes (fully or partially) a line in `plans/future-improvements.md`, or when a tracked plan that originated from the catalog finishes. Agents must not leave catalog bullets describing behavior already on `main`. **No Cursor automation** — this runs as part of wrap-up after every ship."},"2039":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-85","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"**Repos:** Newfin + Rodyna (`plans/future-improvements.md` + `plans/roadmap-index.md`). Jackie-OS: `System/plans/future-improvements.md` + `System/plans/roadmap-index.md`."},"2040":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-86","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"Ship outcome"},"2041":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-87","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"`future-improvements.md`"},"2042":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-88","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"`roadmap-index.md`"},"2043":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-89","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"Fully shipped"},"2044":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-90","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"**Remove** the bullet, or one-line **Shipped baseline** footnote in that section if it helps the next reader"},"2045":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-91","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"Bump `_Last audited…` stamp; add/update **Shipped** table row if major; trim **Genuinely-remaining** / **Near-term ops**"},"2046":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-92","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"Partially shipped"},"2047":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-93","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"Keep bullet; prefix **🔵**; text = gap only (not the whole original scope)"},"2048":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-94","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"🔵 partial on plan row if tracked; refresh remaining-surface blurb"},"2049":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-95","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"Won't do / superseded"},"2050":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-96","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"Remove or move to **Out of scope** with date + reason"},"2051":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-97","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"—"},"2052":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-98","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#steps","content":"Grep `future-improvements.md` for keywords from the ship slice (feature name, route, migration)."},"2053":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-99","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#steps","content":"Verify against code — same discipline as verify-plan doc; **code wins**."},"2054":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-100","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#steps","content":"Edit catalog: no stale \"not started\" lines for live behavior; never archive `future-improvements.md`."},"2055":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-101","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#steps","content":"Update `roadmap-index.md` audit stamp + remaining-surface paragraph in the **same commit**."},"2056":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-102","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#steps","content":"If the slice was large, make sure `decisions-log.md` captures any durable decision (git history holds the blow-by-blow) — catalog cleanup still required either way."},"2057":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-103","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#steps","content":"**Commit in the code repo** with roadmap reconcile (step 8 above). Morning-brief project-sync does **not** edit `plans/` — only agents do."},"2058":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-104","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#process","content":"**Project sync** — always (even if this session only touched an external code repo or `Projects/` folder). Syncs all registry rows: git repos, `STATUS.md` files, vault notes, `hot.md`, and ops-board project lanes when enabled."},"2059":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-105","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#process","content":"**Ops board** — when `Vault/Ops/Bases/Work.base` exists, follow wrap-up (tasks: `doing`→`done`; plans: ship → `status: done` + `done:` date; new catalog rows → plan notes in **backlog**). Move shipped `*-done-*` cards to `Vault/Ops/Archive/Tasks/` or `Archive/Plans/` — never leave done cards in live folders.\r\n2b. **Status trim** — when any active project note's `## Status` exceeds \\~80 lines, run status-archive (keep 5 newest blocks) before commit."},"2060":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-106","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#process","content":"**Status (local)** — if this session changed something project-sync didn't capture (judgment, blockers, decisions, smokes, shipped slices), **prepend** the relevant vault note `## Status` (e.g. Jackie OS, Newfin, Rodyna). Date each entry. Litmus: would this belong in tomorrow's brief **Yesterday · Work**? If yes, it belongs here tonight — not only in `hot.md` or `## Log`."},"2061":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-107","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#process","content":"**Log** — append a timestamped one-liner to today's brief (`Vault/Briefs/YYYY-MM-DD brief.md`) under `## Log` (create the section if missing). If no brief exists, skip."},"2062":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-108","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags"